  "name": "MEAN CORPUSCULAR HAEMOGLOBIN CONCENTRATION (MCHC)",
  "code": "1566",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>It measures the <strong data-start=\"1983\" data-end=\"2014\">concentration of hemoglobin</strong> inside a given volume of RBCs, expressed in g/dL.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>MCHC Result</th>\n<th>Interpretation</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Low (&lt;32 g/dL)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Hypochromia</strong> &ndash; RBCs contain less hemoglobin concentration. Common in iron deficiency anemia, thalassemia.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Normal (32&ndash;36 g/dL)</strong></td>\n<td>Normal hemoglobin concentration.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>High (&gt;36 g/dL)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Hyperchromia</strong> &ndash; often seen in <strong>hereditary spherocytosis</strong> or <strong>autoimmune hemolytic anemia</strong>. Can also occur due to lab artifact (e.g., cold agglutinins, hemolysis, lipemia).</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
